  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Calculate, correct to two decimal places, the mean and standard deviation for each data set.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$3, 5, 6, 10, 12, 14, 11, 12, 11, 15, 5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\bar{x}=9.45,\\quad \\sigma=3.85$",
          "worked": "There are $11$ values, with sum $104$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bar{x}&=\\frac{104}{11}\\\\\\bar{x}&\\approx9.45\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the exact mean, square each value's deviation from $\\frac{104}{11}$ and add the squares:\n$$\\sum (x-\\bar{x})^2=\\frac{1790}{11}.$$\nDivide by the number of values and take the square root:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1790/11}{11}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx3.85\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 16, 18, 12, 11, 10, 14, 16, 18, 19$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\bar{x}=13.50,\\quad \\sigma=3.54$",
          "worked": "There are $14$ values, with sum $189$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bar{x}&=\\frac{189}{14}\\\\\\bar{x}&=13.50\\end{align*}$$\nSquare each value's deviation from $13.5$ and add the squares:\n$$\\sum (x-\\bar{x})^2=175.5.$$\nDivide by the number of values and take the square root:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{175.5}{14}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx3.54\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
